ion.org}]","organiser":"[{Abdullah Gulab}{mailto:agulab@worldcubeassociation.org}] [{Alyssa Esparaz}{mailto:aesparaz@speedcubingcanada.org}] [{Jonathan Esparaz}{mailto:jesparaz@worldcubeassociation.org}] [{Liam Orovec}{mailto:lorovec@worldcubeassociation.org}] [{Michael Zheng}{mailto:mzheng1@worldcubeassociation.org}] [{Sarah Strong}{mailto:sstrong@worldcubeassociation.org}] [{Speedcubing Canada}{mailto:info@speedcubingcanada.org}] [{Tarandeep Mittal}{mailto:tmittal@worldcubeassociation.org}]","venue":{"name":"[George Ashe Library](https:\/\/pickeringlibrary.ca\/locations\/PC\/)","address":"470 Kingston Rd, Pickering, ON","details":"Paris & Franklin Rooms","coordinates":{"latitude":43.812401,"longitude":-79.125129}},"information":"[![](https:\/\/www.worldcubeassociation.org\/rails\/active_storage\/blobs\/redirect\/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBcGd3IiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--413963af1d32608ec1038d304a181c8adedb8510\/SpeedcubingCanadaLogo-724.png)](https:\/\/www.speedcubingcanada.org\/)\r\n\r\n## Blindfolded events only\r\n\r\nThe only events at this competition are ***blindfolded events***, which require a significant amount of practice and concentration. All attendees, including competitors and guests, are asked to please remain quiet at this competition to allow competitors to concentrate.\r\n\r\n## Other competitions\r\n\r\n[FMC Canada 2023](https:\/\/www.worldcubeassociation.org\/competitions\/FMCCanada2023) (Pickering location) and [Please Be Solved Pickering Evening 2023](https:\/\/www.worldcubeassociation.org\/competitions\/PBSPickeringEvening2023) will take place at the same venue, later in the day _after_ this competition. Each competition will end before the next competition begins, ensuring no overlap. Please feel free to register for one or multiple competitions, but **you must register for each competition separately**.\r\n\r\n### Note for new competitors\r\n\r\nAlthough first-timers are welcome to compete if they know how to solve p